///|
/// WMA v2 encoder interop test, pinned byte-for-byte against the stock
/// FFmpeg 9.0.2 `wmav2` encoder.
///
/// Regeneration: the six tone frames come from `wma_enc_test_tone_frame`
/// (wma_encode_wbtest.mbt); the packets are the MoonBit encoder's output
/// for them at 128 kbit/s / 44.1 kHz / stereo, and the reference PCM is the
/// docker `linuxserver/ffmpeg:9.0.2` decode of the SAME byte stream:
///   ffmpeg -v error -y -f s16le -ar 44100 -ac 2 -i wma_ref_input.pcm -c:a wmav2 -b:a 128k -f asf wma_ref.wma
///   ffmpeg -v error -y -i wma_ref.wma -f s16le wma_ref_dec.pcm
/// The MoonBit packets are bit-identical to the ASF payloads in
/// wma_ref.wma (verified offset-by-offset), so this also pins that the
/// C decoder accepts our stream.  The decoded PCM comparison allows the
/// +-1 LSB f32/f64 quantization-boundary residual.

